                <html>
                    <body style = "font-size: 100%;font-weight:bold">
                        <center>Eligibility Risk Based Reviews Policy</center>    
                    </body>
                    <apex:outputPanel rendered="{!isDateAfter_15June2025 == false}">
                        <tr align="left"><td style= "font-size: 100%;" align="left">Sampling Decisions</td></tr>
                        <table border="1" class="list" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" width="100%">
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"> <td width="70%">1. Selection of Cases </td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1__c}<BR/>{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_1__c}</td></tr>
                            <apex:outputPanel rendered="{! CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_1__c == 'Cluster'}" layout="none">
                                <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"> <td width="70%">Clearly describe the population sampled:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_1D__c}</td></tr>
                            </apex:outputPanel>
                            <apex:outputPanel rendered="{! CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_1__c == 'Stratified'}" layout="none">
                                <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"> <td width="70%">Clearly describe the group within the population sampled and if the sample will be random or systematic: </td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_1D__c}</td></tr>
                            </apex:outputPanel>
                            <apex:outputPanel rendered="{! CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_1__c == 'Systematic'}" layout="none">
                                <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"> <td width="70%">Clearly describe the process the County will use to establish the systematic sample (selecting every ___ element):</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_1D__c}</td></tr>
                            </apex:outputPanel>
                            <apex:outputPanel rendered="{! CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1__c == 'The County will establish its own random sample report based on the following: (choose one)'}" layout="none">
                                <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"> <td colspan="2" width="100%">1.1 Ensure the sample meets the state-defined case review standards.</td></tr>
                                <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"> <td width="70%">Ensure a sufficient number of CCCAP cases and/or provider files are reviewed on a monthly basis.</td><td width="30%">Acknowledged</td></tr>
                                <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"> <td width="70%">Maintain a list of the monthly sample of cases/providers in an approved, automated format that is accessible as needed by CCCAP.</td><td width="30%">Acknowledged</td></tr>
                            </apex:outputPanel>
                        </table>
                    </apex:outputPanel>
                </html>
                <apex:outputPanel rendered="{!isDateAfter_15June2025 == false}">
                    <html>
                        <tr align="left"><td style= "font-size: 100%;" align="left">Assurances and Certifications</td></tr>
                        <table border="1" class="list" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" width="100%">
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"> <td width="70%">
                                The County assures that it will abide by the instructions contained in the CCCAP County Review Framework and CCCAP Instruction Guide for County Reviews.<BR/>
                                The data collection process, to include case and provider reviews, adhered to all CCCAP regulations outlined in 8 CCR 1403-1 and applicable state memos and CCCAP training documents that direct program administration.<BR/>
                                The reviews were not conducted by persons who make or approve eligibility determinations or who are under the supervision of persons responsible for eligibility determinations.<BR/>
                                All reviewers have been trained to ensure that the review process is consistent with CCCAP policies and that there is consistency within the county in the interpretation of what is an error as defined by CCCAP.<BR/>
                                The County agrees to retain County Record Review Worksheets, the CCCAP County Review Performance Report and any revisions, and any other records pertinent to the case reviews and submission of error rate reports for three years.<BR/>
                                The County understands that this information, including the sampled case records and calculations, is subject to state review.
                                </td><td width="30%">Acknowledged</td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>
                    </html>                    
                </apex:outputPanel>
                <html>
                    <tr align="left"><td style= "font-size: 100%;" align="left">County Review Plan</td></tr>
                    <table border="1" class="list" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" width="100%">
                        <apex:outputPanel rendered="{!isDateAfter_15June2025 == false}">
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"> <td colspan="2" width="100%">2. Identification of Review Leadership<BR/>Review leaders have the authority to ensure timelines are met. The level of authority should be comparable to that of the leader who is responsible for the oversight of eligibility determinations or provider payments. The leaders identified below do not need to be CHATS users but must understand the Program. Please include the name(s) and job title(s), of each staff member identified in your County that are responsible for leading the following county-level review roles:</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Leader: Monitors timelines and directs county activities and responses in alignment with state and county policies.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_1_1__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Team Coordination Lead: Understands the program, monitors timelines, ensures inter-reviewer consistency, and directs case review process and standards to ensure alignment with state and county policies.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_1_2__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Review Certification Lead: Confirms the accuracy and completeness of the reviews and submits the sampled reviews monthly.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_1_3__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">2.1 Inter-Reviewer Consistency</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">The County will be asked to identify the actions taken to resolve errors identified during the county-level review process as well as the actions taken to prevent future errors. The County will have (20) business days from the date the CCCAP County Review Performance Report is provided to the County to resolve errors identified as part of the review process. If the action to correct the case results in a benefit to the client and/or a decrease to the parent fee) or at the next re-determination. If the action to correct the case does not benefit the client, the information related to the error must be documented in CHATS Case Notes for review at the next re-determination of eligibility. This includes errors that occurred outside of the sample month which were identified as part of the review but did not result in a finding. Documentation of follow up on findings identified during the review by the County must be included in the CCCAP County Review Performance Report submitted by each county.
                                <BR/>
                                Select and describe methods the county will use to ensure inter-reviewer consistency.</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">2.1.1 Re-review of cases to ensure inter-reviewer consistency. Describe:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_2_1D__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">2.1.2 Group discussion of case review findings. Describe:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_2_2D__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">2.1.3 Other, describe:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_2_3D__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">2.2 Review Team Composition</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_3__c}</td></tr>
                            <apex:outputPanel rendered="{!(CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_3__c == 'The County will be conducting its own reviews and will not partner with another county to complete peer reviews.')}" layout="none">
                                <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">If the county will be conducting their own reviews as checked above, please describe the review team by providing information about the following:</td><td width="30%">Size:{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_3_1__c}<BR/>Composition:{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_3_2__c}</td></tr>
                            </apex:outputPanel>
                            <apex:outputPanel rendered="{!(CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_3__c == 'The County will coordinate with another county to conduct reviews based on county size and/or conflicts in the review process.')}" layout="none">
                                <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Please identify the other county(ies) the County will coordinate with to conduct case reviews:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_3_3__c}</td></tr>
                            </apex:outputPanel>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">2.3 Plan for Review of State Policies/Procedures and Processes</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">2.3.1 The County will NOT customize the County Record Review Worksheet for the county-level case and provider reviews.</td><td width="30%">Acknowledged</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">2.3.2 The County would like to customize the County Record Review Worksheet as follows:</td><td width="30%">Acknowledged</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Describe the County’s plan to ensure that customization of the County Record Review Worksheet will follow the CCCAP County Review Framework and CCCAP policy in effect during the sample month:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_4_2D__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">2.3.3 The County will NOT customize the elements, questions, or standards on the County Record Review Worksheet.
                                <BR/>Describe the County’s plan to ensure that reviewers consistently interpret errors as defined by CCCAP: The County is expected to utilize CCCAP standards and training to provide instruction to reviewers so that there is a consistent interpretation of an error. CCCAP has established the state definitions for errors, improper payment errors, and administrative errors as follows:</td><td width="30%">Acknowledged</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Error- any variance that results in inaccurate eligibility based on policy or regulation, which may or may not affect the child care authorization or subsidy paid to the provider.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_4_31D__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Improper Payment Error- any variance that results in inaccurate eligibility based on policy or regulation, which causes a difference in the subsidy payment that is greater than $0.99. The impact could be positive or negative.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_4_32D__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Administrative (Non-payment) Error- any variance that results in inaccurate eligibility based on policy or regulation, which does not affect the child care authorization or subsidy paid to the provider.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_4_33D__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">2.4 Case Review Logistics</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Describe details of review logistics to include the following: whether electronic or physical record is reviewed, how the records (especially the physical records) are handled, where the record reading occurs (on-site, centrally, regionally, a mixture), the organization and maintenance of the review files:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_5__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">2.5 Plan for Follow Up on Findings</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Describe the County’s plan to ensure that cases with errors are corrected: The County will create reports based on the data collected in the CCCAP County Review Performance Report and include statewide and county level performance indicators and top error trends. The data will be compiled into reports to address the primary cause of the top error trends, identify if the county needs additional technical assistance and/or support, and identify future training needs.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_6__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">2.5.1 If findings result in the creation of new policies and procedures, describe the County’s plan to:</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Incorporate the changes:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_6_1__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Train staff regarding the changes:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_6_2__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Evaluate the changes to determine if they were effective:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_6_3__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Monitor to ensure the changes are integrated into the County’s business processes:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_6_4__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">2.6 Plan for Data Collection (Monthly Submission of County Review Results</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Describe the County’s plan to ensure that the data entered in the CCCAP County Review Performance Report is accurate, the data has been validated, and the coding is correct based on the instructions and standards outlined in the CCCAP County Review Framework and CCCAP Instruction Guide for County Reviews:</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_7__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">2.6.1 Name, job title, and email of the person who will certify and submit the monthly CCCAP County Review Performance Report:</td><td width="30%">Name: {!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_7_1__c}<br/>Title: {!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_7_2__c}<br/>Email: {!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q3_7_3__c}</td></tr>
                        </apex:outputPanel>
                        <apex:outputPanel rendered="{!isDateAfter_15June2025 == true}">
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">1. Inter-Reviewer Consistency</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Select the methods the county will use to ensure inter-reviewer consistency.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_new__c}</td></tr>
                            <apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_new__c == 'Other'}" layout="none">
                                <tr style="{!IF(ISBLANK(CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_other__c),'display:none;','')}" class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">If other, please specify.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_other__c}</td></tr>
                            </apex:outputPanel>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">1.1 Case Review Logistics</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Does the county have electronic or physical records?</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_1_new__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Where does the record review occur?</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_2_new__c}</td></tr>
                            <apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_2_new__c == 'Offsite'}" layout="none">
                                <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Describe how the county ensures that the physical records remain secure during transport to the offsite location before the are reviewed.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q1_2_other__c}</td></tr>
                            </apex:outputPanel>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td colspan="2" width="100%">2. Plan for Follow Up on Findings</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">Describe the County’s plan to ensure that cases with errors are corrected: The County must create reports based on the data collected in the CCCAP County Review Performance Report and include statewide and county level performance indicators and top error trends. Indicate the number of business days in which the county will correct the errors.</td>
                                <td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q2_1__c}</td></tr>
                            <tr class="dataRow" width="100%"><td width="70%">If findings result in the creation of new policies and procedures, describe the County’s plan to incorporate the changes, including training staff, evaluating the effectiveness of the changes, and ensuring that staff consistently apply the new policies and procedures.</td><td width="30%">{!CountyPlan.RBRP_Q2_2__c}</td></tr>
                        </apex:outputPanel>
                    </table>
                </html>
            </apex:pageBlockSection>
        </apex:pageBlock>
